<title>USA: U.S. Congressman wants meat inspection changes.</title>
<headline>U.S. Congressman wants meat inspection changes.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Rep. Jim Lightfoot (R-Ia) called on the Agriculture Department to address the differences in inspection regulations between meat and poultry.</p>
<p>In a letter, Lightfoot asked Agriculture Secretary Dan Glickman to start rulemaking procedures to address the differences.</p>
<p>&quot;These disparities provide an estimated $3 billion economic advantage to the poultry industry,&quot; Lightfoot said in his letter.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
</text>
